# Trivy ignore file for the CodeQ CLI dependency security gate.
#
# This file is consumed by the qbraid-infrastructure Cloud Build triggers
# (opencode-staging-branch / opencode-prod-main) which scan ONLY the shipped
# CodeQ CLI dependency closure (see script/cli-scan-manifest.ts).
#
# Every entry MUST carry a justification and be re-evaluated on dependency bumps.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# undici 5.29.0 — three WebSocket-related Denial-of-Service CVEs.
#
# undici reaches the shipped binary ONLY transitively via
#   @actions/github -> @actions/http-client
# which pins undici "^5" and uses it strictly as an HTTP(S) client for GitHub
# REST calls in `codeq github` mode. All three CVEs are in undici's WebSocket /
# permessage-deflate handling, which the CLI never invokes. Fixes exist only in
# undici 6.27+/7.28+/8.5+; forcing a major bump breaks @actions/http-client's
# undici 5.x API. Re-evaluate if @actions/github releases a version that bumps
# undici past 5.x.
CVE-2026-12151
CVE-2026-1526
CVE-2026-2229

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# seroval 1.4.1 — CVE-2026-59940 (CRITICAL): `seroval.fromJSON()` Promise
# resolver type confusion invokes attacker-controlled methods during
# deserialization.
#
# TEMPORARY — unlike the undici entries above, a fix IS available (seroval
# 1.5.3) and the bump is a one-line change to the existing root `overrides`
# pin. Tracked in qBraid/opencode#44; remove this entry when that lands.
#
# seroval reaches the shipped binary ONLY transitively via
#   @opentui/solid -> solid-js -> seroval
# and is pinned to a single resolution by the root package.json `overrides`
# block. The vulnerable API, `fromJSON()`, is solid's SSR/hydration payload
# deserializer. The CLI performs no hydration: the shipped source contains no
# `hydrate`, `renderToString`, `renderToStream` or `@solidjs/start` usage, and
# its single `solid-js/web` import is `Dynamic` (a client-side component
# helper) in src/cli/cmd/tui/routes/session/index.tsx. There is therefore no
# call path to `fromJSON()`, and no attacker-supplied serialized payload for
# one to consume.
#
# Suppressed to unblock the codeq staging/prod rollout (qBraid/opencode#16),
# NOT because the risk was judged acceptable long-term.
CVE-2026-59940
